      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "QUICK COOKIE (1) is the horse to beat after being eased from Saturday company, and her last-start Ascot failure reads better than last of eight given she was 1200m to 2200m there. Her second in NMW1Y company two back has substance, while the return to 1500m looks a major key. KIDDING ME (3) brings winning form from this track, having beaten Tora Bora by a length on soft ground, and she is better placed third-up. The rise in trip looks no issue and she can repeat the dose. GOOD SHOW (4) closed off for third in a CL1 at Northam and can hold a placing if he repeats that late work on soft ground. HEY TRUE BLUE (2) has a prior win at this venue and around 1500m, but was beaten just under four lengths as a well-backed BM58+ chance last start. Can play a major role. MORIAH (5) is better than she showed last start and can bounce back to form.",
